addition: Addition means putting numbers together, like 2 plus 3 is 5.
subtraction: Subtraction means taking a number away, like 5 minus 2 is 3.
multiplication: Multiplication means adding a number many times, like 3 times 4 is 12.
division: Division means sharing a number into equal parts, like 12 divided by 3 is 4.
tired: Tired means needing rest or sleep.
thirsty: Thirsty means wanting a drink.
afraid, scared: Afraid or scared means feeling fear.
funny: Funny means making people laugh.
something: Something means a thing that is not named.
nevermind, never mind: Nevermind or never mind means forget it, it does not matter.
okay, ok: Okay or ok means yes, fine or alright.
lol: Lol means laughing out loud.
lmao: Lmao means laughing very hard.
insufferable: Insufferable means very annoying, too much to bear.
unbearable: Unbearable means too hard or too unpleasant to stand.
age: Age means how old someone or something is.
think: To think means to use your mind.
help: To help means to make something easier for someone.
dance: Dance means moving your body to music.
hurt: Hurt means feeling pain, or causing pain.
sick: Sick means not healthy, feeling ill.
painting: A painting is a picture made with paint.
walking: Walking means moving on your feet at a normal speed.
cooking: Cooking means making food ready to eat by heating it.
reading: Reading means looking at written words and understanding them.
writing: Writing means putting words on paper or on a screen.
drawing: Drawing means making a picture with a pen or pencil.
singing: Singing means making music with your voice.
playing: Playing means doing something for fun.
working: Working means doing a job or a task.
talking: Talking means saying words to someone.
listening: Listening means paying attention to sounds or to someone speaking.
speaking: Speaking means saying words out loud.
waiting: Waiting means staying until something happens.
buying: Buying means getting something by paying money.
selling: Selling means giving something to someone for money.
health: Health means how well your body and mind are.
maybe: Maybe means perhaps, it might be or might not be.
sometimes: Sometimes means some of the time.
now: Now means at this moment.
later: Later means at a time after now.
soon: Soon means in a short time.
here: Here means in this place.
there: There means in that place.
fun: Fun means enjoyment, something that makes you happy.
bored: Bored means tired of something because it is not interesting.
lonely: Lonely means sad because you are alone.
proud: Proud means happy about something you or someone close to you did.
worried: Worried means thinking that something bad might happen.
excited: Excited means very happy and full of energy about something.
smart, clever: Smart or clever means able to learn and understand things quickly.
annoying: Annoying means making someone a bit angry or tired of it.
